 To create a list of races per rider using Pro Cycling Stats API, you'll need to iterate through each rider's upcoming participations and extract the race names. Here's how you can do it in Python:

```python
import requests

# Replace 'rider_name' with the name of the desired rider
url = f"https://api.procyclingstats.com/v2/riders/{'rider_name'.replace(' ', '%20')}/upcoming"
headers = {
    'Accept': 'application/json',
}

response = requests.get(url, headers=headers)
data = response.json()
races_per_rider = {}

if data["status"] == 200:
    rider_info = data["data"][0]
    upcoming_participations = rider_info["nextSeasonRaces"]

    for participation in upcoming_participations:
        race_name = participation["event"]["name"]
        if race_name not in races_per_rider:
            races_per_rider[race_name] = []
        races_per_rider[race_name].append(rider_info["id"])

print("Races per rider:")
for race_name, rider_ids in races_per_rider.items():
    print(f"{race_name}: {len(rider_ids)} riders")
else:
    print("Error:", data["message"])
```

