First, install the package using npm or yarn:

```bash
npm install react-break-words
# or
yarn add react-break-words
```

Now, create a custom component called `NoWidows.js`:

```javascript
import React from 'react';
import { Paragraph } from 'react-break-words';

const NoWidows = ({ children }) => (
  <Paragraph className="no-widows">{children}</Paragraph>
);

export default NoWidows;
```

Add the following CSS to your main stylesheet or within the component file to prevent orphans and ensure proper line breaks:

```css
.no-widows {
  hyphens: auto;
  word-wrap: break-word;
  -ms-hyphens: auto; /* For Internet Explorer */
}

/* Optional: If you prefer to have no hyphenation at all */
.no-widows::before {
  content: '\A0';
  height: 1px;
  overflow: hidden;
  white-space: nowrap;
  margin-top: -1px;
}
```

Use the `NoWidows` component wherever you want to avoid widows:

